; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Dina Titus (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Dina Titus seeks another term in a Las Vegas-area district that leans Democratic by a few points. She faces Republican Carrie Buck, who has raised a credible sum, though Titus holds the advantage in cash on hand and the benefits of incumbency. No public general-election polling is available, so the picture rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and market pricing.\n\nRaters overwhelmingly call the race Likely D or safer, with only Inside Elections at Lean D, and prediction markets give Titus roughly a 95% chance. Both party committees have targeted the seat, and headlines note Nevada could complicate a blue wave, but nothing yet suggests a genuine tossup. Titus is favored to win, with Buck needing a strong closing stretch to make it competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 11.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9485, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9231, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9459, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9435, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9451, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9504, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9435, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9463, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9234, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9304, "margin": 10.8}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9333, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9462, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9264, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9326, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.931